    "preamble": "Biju vs State Of Kerala on 17 January, 2024 Author: A. Muhamed Mustaque Bench: A.Muhamed Mustaque IN THE HIGH COURT OF KERALA AT ERNAKULAM PRESENT THE HONOURABLE MR. JUSTICE A.MUHAMED MUSTAQUE & THE HONOURABLE MRS. JUSTICE SHOBA ANNAMMA EAPEN WEDNESDAY, THE 17TH DAY OF JANUARY 2024 / 27TH POUSHA, 1945 WP(C) NO. 37424 OF 2023 PETITIONER/S: 1 BIJU AGED 39 YEARS, S/O.KUMARAN, PUTHENPURACKEL HOUSE, POOPPARA.P.O, POOPPARA VILLAGE, UDUMBANCHOLA THALUK, IDUKKI DISTRICT, PIN - 685619 2 THASHKAND AGED 57 YEARS S/O NAGAYYA, SNP HOUSE, POOPPARA.P.O, POOPPARA VILLAGE, UDUMBANCHOLA THALUK, IDUKKI DISTRICT, PIN - 685619 BY ADVS. C.A.NAVAS T.K.SASIKUMAR LAYA SIMON RAVIVARMA V. RESPONDENT/S: 1 STATE OF KERALA REPRESENTED BY THE SECRETARY, DEPARTMENT OF REVENUE, SECRETARIAT, THIRUVANANTHAPURAM DISTRICT, PIN - 695001 2 THE DISTRICT COLLECTOR IDUKKI, COLLECTORATE, KUYILIMALA, PAINAVU. P.O, IDUKKI DISTRICT, PIN - 685603 WP(C) NO. 37424 OF 2023 ..2.. 3 SUB COLLECTOR Biju vs State Of Kerala on 17 January, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/50326565/ 1 DEVIKULAM, REVENUE DIVISIONAL OFFICE, DEVIKULAM CIRCULAR ROAD, DEVIKULAM TALUK, IDUKKI DISTRICT, PIN - 685613 4 THE TAHSILDAR UDUMBANCHOLA THALUK, UDUMBANCHOLA, IDUKKIO DISTRICT, PIN - 685554 5 THE VILLAGE OFFICER POOPPARA VILLAGE, POOPPARA, IDUKKI DISTRICT, PIN - 685619 6 SHANTHANPARA GRAMA PANCHAYAT, PANCHAYAT OFFICE, SHANTHANPARA, IDUKKI DISTRICT- 685 619 REPRESENTED BY ITS SECRETARY., PIN - 685619 7 THE SECRETARY SHANTHANPARA GRAMA PANCHAYAT, PANCHAYAT OFFICE, SHANTHANPARA, IDUKKI DISTRICT, PIN - 685619 8 K.N.RAJAN AGED 58 YEARS S/O NARAYANAN NAIR, RESIDING AT KANANKUNNATH, SHATHANPARA P.O, THOTTIKKANAM, IDUKKI DISTRICT, PIN - 685619 9 SAJEEV SEBASTIAN AGED 48 YEARS S/O SEBASTIAN, KONDATTUPARAMBIL HOUSE, SHATHANPARA, PUTHADY P.O, RAJAPPARA, IDUKKI DISTRICT, PIN - 685619 ADDL.R10 BASHEER (DELETED) S/O LATE M.A.MUHAMMED, MALIKAKUDIYIL HOUSE, POOPPARA KARA, POOPPARA VILLAGE, UDUMBANCHOLA TALUK, IDUKKI DISTRICT-685619 ADDL.R11 BABU VARGHESE (DELETED) S/O VARGHESE, THAMARAPILLIL HOUSE, POOPPARA P.O., POOPPARA VILLAGE, UDUMBANCHOLA TALUK, IDUKKI DISTRICT -685619 WP(C) NO. 37424 OF 2023 ..3.. ADDL.R12 ADDL.R12.AJAS M.A (DELETED) S/O ABUBAKER, MALIYEKKUDIYIL HOUSE, KULAPPARACHAL P.O., MURIKKINTHOTTI, POOPPARA VILLAGE, UDUMBANCHOLA TALUK, IDUKKI DISTRICT -685619 ADDL.R13 ADDL.R13.M.SELVAM (DELETED) S/O MOKKASAMY THEVAR, ASHOK BHAVAN, PALAM COLONY, POOPPARA, POOPPARA VILLAGE, UDUMBANCHOLA Biju vs State Of Kerala on 17 January, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/50326565/ 2 TALUK, IDUKKI DISTRICT -685619 ADDL.R14 ADDL.R14.AJAYAN (DELETED) S/O RAGHAVAN, CHARUVIL PUTHEN VEEDU, KORANPARA, POOPPARA VILLAGE, UDUMBANCHOLA TALUK, IDUKKI DISTRICT -685619 ADDL.R15 ADDL.R15.BALAMURUGHAN (DELETED) S/O IRULANDI, POPPARA, POOPPARA P.O., POOPPARA VILLAGE, UDUMBANCHOLA TALUK, IDUKKI DISTRICT- 685619 *(ADDITIONAL R10 TO R15 ARE IMPLEADED AS PER ORDER DATED 05.12.2023 IN I.A.1/2023. ** ADDITIONAL R10 TO R15 ARE DELETED AS PER ORDER DATED 10.01.2024 IN I.A.1/2023 IN WP(C). BY ADVS. JOICE GEORGE ASWATHY KRISHNAN LATHEESH SEBASTIAN A.L.NAVANEETH KRISHNAN(K/777/2015) THIS WRIT PETITION (CIVIL) HAVING COME UP FOR ADMISSION ON 17.01.2024, THE COURT ON THE SAME DAY DELIVERED THE FOLLOWING: WP(C) NO. 37424 OF 2023 ..4.. JUDGMENT A. MUHAMED MUSTAQUE, J. This writ petition is filed against land conservancy proceedings. This is a case, where WP(C) NO. Biju vs State Of Kerala on 17 January, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/50326565/ 3 37424 OF 2023 ..5.. the land itself found to be government land and where the encroachers have put up construction.",
    "facts": "Therefore, as per interim order dated 21.11.2023, we directed the revenue officials to initiate action against all other encroachers. 2. The petitioners constructed building encroaching upon the government land with absolutely no semblance of time. The petitioners would say that they have obtained an order from the Tribunal for Local Self Government Institutions as against demolition of the building and therefore, the land conservancy proceedings cannot be initiated. 3. It is to be noted that the challenge before the Tribunal was against the order of the local authority, alleging construction in violation of the Kerala Building Rules.",
    "arguments": ""
